# Logging

Global exception handlers log every `ApplicationException` exactly once, at
the level `Logging Levels` specifies. A use case or repository that is about
to `raise` (or re-raise via `... from exc`) an `ApplicationException` MUST
NOT also call `logger.*` for that same failure — that produces two log
lines for one incident. Attach extra diagnostic fields via `log_context`
instead (see "Log Context vs Details").

Only log directly in a use case when a failure is caught and handled — i.e.
NOT re-raised as an `ApplicationException` — since nothing downstream will
log it otherwise.

Unexpected exceptions

must be logged

by the catch-all handler (`unhandled_exception_handler`, CRITICAL).

