# Cursor and Claude MUST NEVER

Generate HTTPException outside `app/core/exception_handlers.py` (except documented presentation-only cases)

Generate per-endpoint try/except for application exceptions

Generate manual error JSON in routers

Generate generic Exception

Generate bare except

Generate silent exception handling

Generate pass inside except

Generate swallowed exceptions

Generate SQLAlchemy exceptions outside repositories

Generate stack traces in API responses

Generate inconsistent error responses

Generate magic error strings

Generate endpoint-specific error formats

Generate duplicated exception hierarchies

Generate infrastructure exceptions inside Domain

Generate transport exceptions inside Domain

Generate print() for errors

Generate sensitive information inside messages

Generate rollback inside repositories

Generate a `logger.*` call in a use case or repository for an `ApplicationException` that is about to propagate or be re-raised

Generate internal-only diagnostic fields (ids, driver text) inside `details` — use `log_context`

Generate raw `exc.errors()` (with `input` intact) into a log call or response body

