# Final Principle

Errors are domain concepts, not implementation details.

Infrastructure failures should be translated into application exceptions.

Global exception handlers should translate application exceptions into HTTP responses with the standard envelope.

Clients should never know whether a failure originated from SQLAlchemy, MySQL, Redis, RabbitMQ, or any other internal component.

A well-designed error system makes failures predictable, secure, observable, and easy to maintain.